# 0103 WIP: EP0 robustness on the device side.
#
# Four host-visible weaknesses were fixed:
#  1. EP0 setup capture stalled on the first short RXCOUNT0 read; at full
#     speed a SETUP packet can still be arriving, so the read is now retried
#     for a bounded window before the request is stalled.
#  2. The host resets the bus whenever an enumeration attempt fails.  The
#     MAC2 common-USB status latches that event; the driver now polls it and
#     recovers (device address back to 0, EP0 re-armed, EP2/QMU stopped),
#     so the host's next attempt is not answered by a stale state machine.
#  3. EP0 is armed and the reset flag is latched before the pull-up makes
#     the device visible, closing the window where the host could talk to an
#     EP0 that was not ready yet.
#  4. The VBUS sense is polled (debounced) so a physical unplug is noticed
#     and the next attach re-arms the device; this is the retry path that
#     does not need a reboot.  The PHY is not re-initialised here: whether
#     the session survives the unplug is measured by the "VBUS attached,
#     device re-armed" log line, and a PHY re-init is a separate change.
#
# EP2 QMU behaviour (0095-0102) is unchanged; the reset recovery stops the
# TX QMU and lets the next SET_CONFIGURATION reconfigure it.

MACOS_VERSION=13.5
KERNEL_CONFIG=DEVELOPMENT
MACHINE_CONFIG=SWEET

BASE_REPO=https://github.com/MakrSas/ios-topaz.git
BASE_SHA=5095ac19dbdcf37b64b81fe443f4027ad51b84bf
PATCHSET_SHA256=eab46845f36523ce24be2d1957c924dfc9d429fb6db863abe68211c4fbc69708
BASELINE_CHANGES_SHA256=1edb66332bb4daa8b1abcd6c4de77a0e88ed9c7e9bb4a2a7045a2696e53ab338

DXB_REPO=https://github.com/blacktop/darwin-xnu-build
DXB_SHA=663906528d1cd5ea8fde7de6f16de73db9511549

KERNEL_EXPECT_EXEC_DATA=
CI_RUN_ID=
CI_KERNEL_SHA256=
CI_KERNEL_EXEC_DATA_SHA256=
CI_IMAGE_SHA256=

BOOT_CMDLINE=config/0103-boot.cmdline
